    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the suite, and it passes. `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`BuildOwner.java`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`):\n- `nextCustomerCode` now takes the city as well and produces `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n  - `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city.\n  - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of the last name (extracted via a shared `prefix3` helper).\n  - `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of existing owners in that city (was a global count), matching city case-insensitively.\n- Updated the call site to pass `owner.getCity()` and the Javadoc.\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode`:** the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is built at mapping time by appending `-M<YY>` to `getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`) with no code change needed. No other derived values exist.\n\n**`openapi.yml`:** updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions/examples to reflect the new format.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` \u2014 which asserts `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` \u2014 now passes, and the full suite is green.",
